Z||000008||anthony_86gt||02-14-2001||06:49 PM||||im from monroe county, MI.  where are you from knight??  i have a 86.5 gt, where is the water trap???<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||02-14-2001||08:48 PM||||I am definitely seeing increased gas milage, but the seat-o-the-pants meter has not registered any performance gains...<P>Wait for a discount code and order your K&N from carparts.com.  <P>(Cooter, theres the other subject that will open up ye old can of worms)<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||02-15-2001||01:50 AM||||The Fiero air intake is already very efficient, so a K&N isn't going to give much of a performance increase. On some vehicles with poorly designed intakes, adding a K&N gives a fairly big increase in available power, but again, it's simply replacing a restrictive intake. On a system that's already able to suck all the air it needs, it won't do much.<BR>On the other hand, K&N filters practically last forever.. It will need periodic cleaning, but but not replacement.. <P>I wouldn't expect any increases in power from it, but I say go for it, and get the K&N..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000011||1FST2M6||02-15-2001||08:01 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BlackGTdyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BlackGTdyno.jpg</A> <P>dyno results of BlackGTs 86 GT 4spd.  The K&N is worht the money cause it'll last longer than you'll have the car. and the added HP is just a bonus. K&N part # E-0890  usually about $25<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||fierogt88||02-15-2001||08:38 AM||||After reading a week-long flame war on the fiero mailing list on this topic, I thought I might share with you the general consensus that was left after all the smoke cleared...<P>A) It's worth the money because it will last you forever.  As soon as you need a replacement, go ahead and get one.<P>B) It will not give you any performance increase on a stock car, but it can help once other performance bottlenecks have been addressed.<P>This is just my summarization of the opinions of many people with lots more experience than me, so point that flamethrower away from me, please  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||1FST2M6||02-15-2001||10:40 AM||||what list? 1.5hp and 3.3lbft is an improvement it's much better than a spiral-max...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000014||stimpy||02-15-2001||10:50 AM||||I have a low-restriction exhaust and upgraded ignition. My Ass-O-Meter felt more urgent low-end acceleration after the K&N was installed. I don't feel at all cheated for the $25 I spent on it.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Voytek||02-15-2001||12:18 PM||||Not entirely true that you'll never again spend any money on a filter.  The K&N needs re-oiling every time you clean it.  You need to buy a kit for it and p*ss around with it every time your filter gets dirty.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Carrolles||02-15-2001||12:56 PM||||Take a look at this article to see what is said about the stock Fiero v-6 intake system.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.org/text/firedup.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.org/text/firedup.txt</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||ThatRickGuy||02-15-2001||01:17 PM||||"God and religion, favorite spark plugs, which oil is best, where to get your oil changed and of course removing a cat. converter. <BR>Back to the question- For performance, maybe not. Never having to buy another air filter, a definate yes."<P>Yes and no, anything with the right gap, 5w-30 Gastrol, do it yourself, hack saw and a hammer.<P>okay, as for the K&N, and other intake dealings. The K&N is worth the money just for the fact that you'll never have to replace it. As for the HP gain, it's not going to be anything major, but the do flow better then most disposable filters. And removing the water trap does not help air flow. The box was put there by someone with a PHD, taking it off is from somone else 'with a good idea'. Personally, I trust the PHD :P<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||LarryB||02-15-2001||01:30 PM||||What's the accuracy of the dyno?  The differences between the quoted figures is less than 2%, and if the tolerance spec is near or greater than that figure you can't draw many valid conclusions (other than the results appear to be about the same within 2%), especially since there was only 1 test with each configuration run. <P>It sure looks like (unlike a lot of stuff that gets peddled) at the very least a properly installed and maintained new filter won't hurt anything and might even help a bit under the right conditions, so if you wanted one even just for the looks I'd say just go for it. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>what list? 1.5hp and 3.3lbft is an improvement it's much better than a spiral-max...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||4
Z||000019||rogergarrison||02-15-2001||02:16 PM||||what I found about the OEM paper filter is since moisture gets in the filter canister the paper degrades pretty fast to a gob of wet paper. Thats why I went to K&N.||||reg||1
Z||000020||1FST2M6||02-15-2001||03:31 PM||||there was more than one run just those two were selected..  that car was flogged for about an hour with no wind and with a 30mph wind.. and those shown are the best ones that Todds car laid down. the dyno is VERY consistant. the motors and cars aren't. tranny temps, heat soak on the blocks tire temps all play a factor... all the dyno runs were within .8hp of the other... the first ones were higher cause the air temps and intake system temps were low... but even after the last pulls the K&N always made more HP and TQ.  as for that article.. they never take into account air pressure on the car at a given speed.. we have a 6 sensor manometer from Devilbiss (the car painting people) that measures the air pressures at any given point they are small probes about 1/2 the size of a pencil. with a 45mph wind down the side of the car the HP was up with the removal and replacement of the stock air box with a piece of 2.5" aluminum piping into the stock air filter canister and silicon sealing so the only air was the inlet on the outside and the TB. we realized a hp gain in our testing. however with the stock unit we noticed only a decrease in intake air temps and no pressure change in the intake system.. but no HP increase.<P>just our findings... <P><BR>oh and the "stock" filter was a new out of the box NAPA filter never used just like the K&N... of course a K&N will make more HP than a dirty old nasty paper one...<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||Alex4mula||02-15-2001||03:50 PM||||I love when people talk with data  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> My K&N has 10 years of use. Still as good as original. If you can afford it buy it. You won't regret.||||reg||1
Z||000022||c m west||02-16-2001||08:05 PM||||Here at West Coast Fiero we can Supply you with out Velocity Tube kit that replaces the existing restrictive intake. Our Velocity Tube features K&N Filterchargers, as well as other K&N types which offer a wide range of colors, visible through the driver side intake vent on the Fiero when using the Velocity Tube - check us out at <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <P>Eric - West Coast Fiero              ||||reg||1
